# Commits that `git blame` skips, so that it shows the commit that last
# changed what a line does, not one that only changed its layout. GitHub reads
# this file by itself. Locally, once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# Add only commits whose code changes are layout only (full SHA, the one that
# landed on main, with a comment naming its pull request). Blame skips the
# whole commit, so any config or doc lines it changed are skipped too.

